WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:08.470
This is Arya Stark in Game of Thrones season
one, in season three, in season five. What

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:13.940
happened? And what’ll happen next? Let’s
work it out. Arya is the daughter of Ned Stark

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.119
and Catelyn Tully. At the start of the series
she’s a scrawny little nine-year old girl,

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:22.529
and a bit of a “wild” child, “fierce”
and “willful”. While her older sister

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:27.719
Sansa plays the part of a lady, dressing nicely,
speaking politely, learning to sew and sing,

00:00:27.719 --> 00:00:33.060
Arya likes to fight and ride and explore. She doesn’t “want to be” “the highborn

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.670
lady [she’s] supposed to be”, so she
“never seem[s] to fit” – a bit like

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:42.239
Jon Snow, who she has a “close” relationship
with. Jon gives Arya her little sword, Needle,

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:48.449
before going away to the Wall. Arya also “love[s]”
her direwolf, Nymeria, but has to send her

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:53.219
away after an incident with Joffrey, which
also leads to the death of Sansa’s direwolf,

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:57.570
under the orders of Queen Cersei, and the
death of Arya’s friend Mycah, at the hands

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:05.019
of the Hound, filling Arya with guilt and
grief, anger and hate. At King’s Landing,

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:10.580
Syrio Forel teaches Arya to fight, and to
be strong, perceptive, agile, quick and fearless.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:16.300
So Arya trains, chases cats, overhears a
very interesting chat, and eventually everything

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.610
starts going wrong again. King Robert dies, Lannisters kill Starks, and Syrio seemingly

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:27.030
sacrifices himself to save Arya. Arya kills
a boy on the way out of the Red Keep, then

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:32.970
lives rough in King’s Landing until she
witnesses the death of Ned Stark. So in the

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:38.280
first book and season of Game of Thrones,
Arya’s friend, her teacher, and her father

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:43.860
are all killed. She’s separated from her
family, her direwolf and her life as a highborn.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.850
All her grief becomes hatred for the people
who caused these things, she wants them dead,

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:54.810
but is powerless to do anything against
them. For now.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.440
Arya tries to return to the north with a group
of Night’s Watch recruits. She assumes

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.310
the identity of a boy named Arry, and makes
friends with Gendry, Hot Pie and Lommy. But

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:08.500
the group is attacked by Amory Lorch, forcing
Arya and her friends to fight and flee – on

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.860
the way Arya frees the mysterious Jaqen H’ghar.
Arya and co. are captured by Gregor Clegane,

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:22.170
Lommy is killed, and they’re taken to Harrenhal. Arya sees horrible things at Harrenhal.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:27.200
Murder, torture, rape. She’s meets many
of the worst people in Westeros – Amory

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.930
Lorch, Gregor Clegane, the Brave Companions,
Tywin Lannister, Roose Bolton. Arya starts

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:37.920
to lose touch with her identity. Induction
to Harrenhal is like joining the military

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.370
or a cult. She’s stripped and scrubbed and
has her hair cut, has the “pride” and

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:47.700
“defiance” beaten out of her, and is worked
hard. To survive in Harrenhal, she can’t

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.960
be “wild Arya”, or “fierce” Arry.
She becomes a “grey mouse girl”, called

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.260
Weasel , “ke[eping] to the crannies and
crevices … of the castle”. When Roose

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:01.209
Bolton takes Harrenhal, she takes the name
Nymeria, or Nan, and thinks she’s “not

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.370
even [herself any more]”. One of the few
things connecting her to her to her identity

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:11.090
as Arya is her hatred for the people she wants
dead. She thinks about them as she works,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:16.890
lists them in her “prayer” before sleep, constantly broods on killing and hate. Jaqen

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:21.290
H’ghar turns up and tells Arya that since
she saved him and his companions, he owes

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:26.990
a sort of death debt, so he kills people for
her. This “ma[kes Arya] brave again”,

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:31.840
“a ghost instead of a mouse”. When Jaqen
leaves, he gives her a coin, and the words

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:37.849
“Valar morghulis” – all men must die. Arya escapes Harrenhal with Hot Pie and

00:03:37.849 --> 00:03:43.040
Gendry, killing a guard on the way out. So
in this book, Arya moves closer to violence

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.520
and hate, and begins to separate from her
identity.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:53.680
At start of Book and Season 3, Arya is free
from the horrors of Harrenhal. She rides

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.709
for Riverrun, to find Robb and Catelyn, but
she’s captured by the Brotherhood Without

00:03:57.709 --> 00:04:02.819
Banners, an outlaw group ostensibly fighting
to “defend the realm”. She sees the trial

00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:06.690
of the Hound and the resurrection of Beric
Dondarrion, and though the Brotherhood promise

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:12.440
to take Arya to her mother, that never ends
up happening. Hot Pie starts work at an inn,

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:17.599
and Gendry joins the Brotherhood, leaving
Arya feeling abandoned and betrayed. She

00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:21.989
wants people she can trust, a family, what
she calls a “pack”, and she doesn’t

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:28.139
find it with the Brotherhood, so she runs
away, and is caught by the Hound, Sandor Clegane.

00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:32.529
The Hound takes her across the riverlands,
trying and failing to ransom her off. They

00:04:32.529 --> 00:04:38.419
kill Freys and Lannisters together, and develop
this wonderful complicated friendship. Arya

00:04:38.419 --> 00:04:42.569
hates the Hound for killing Mycah, and goes
on and on about how she’s gonna kill him,

00:04:42.569 --> 00:04:46.449
or run away, but she never does, even though she gets lots of opportunities.

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:51.129
The Hound says he only keeps Arya around
so he can sell her off, but even after that

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:57.259
fails and she’s not worth anything to him
anymore, he stays with her. Why? Arya and

00:04:57.259 --> 00:05:02.539
the Hound are very very similar. They’ve
both suffered, both been forced to serve terrible

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:07.479
men doing terrible things, both feel betrayed
by their siblings. They’re both cynical

00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:12.449
and angry and “hateful”. They hate Joffrey,
they hate Cersei, they hate Gregor, they

00:05:12.449 --> 00:05:17.459
hate cowards, they hate liars. They both
use literal disguises that hide their faces

00:05:17.459 --> 00:05:22.599
– and they use symbolic disguises in that
they both act tough, threatening people, boasting

00:05:22.599 --> 00:05:26.409
about killing, acting like they need no one, and killing makes them happy, when in

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:32.789
truth, they are afraid, they feel pain, they
cry. They have no families to speak of, no

00:05:32.789 --> 00:05:38.400
homes, nowhere to go. They say they don’t
care about each other, but clearly they do.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.589
They have no one else. So when Arya refuses
to give Sandor the gift of mercy, maybe that

00:05:43.589 --> 00:05:49.789
was spite for killing Mycah. But maybe, Arya
couldn’t bring herself to kill her only

00:05:49.789 --> 00:05:55.789
friend. Anyway. With no one and no reason
left to stay in Westeros, Arya sails to Braavos,

00:05:55.789 --> 00:06:03.479
clinging to the last thing she has left – her
will to kill the people in her prayer.

00:06:03.479 --> 00:06:08.430
In Braavos, Arya uses Jaqen’s coin to join
the Faceless Men, a cult of assassins who

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:14.129
worship death. To truly become a Faceless
Man, Arya must let go of her identity, of

00:06:14.129 --> 00:06:19.009
her “hopes and dreams, [her] loves and hates
… [of] all that makes [her] who [she is]”.

00:06:19.009 --> 00:06:24.650
Arya must become “No one”. Arya works
sweeping floors, and cleaning corpses. Under

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.830
the name of Cat she spends time in the city,
learning the language, and the Faceless Men

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:33.339
teach her to lie. She’s later made blind,
and given the name Beth, in the books not

00:06:33.339 --> 00:06:38.639
so much as a punishment as part of her training,
to develop all her senses. After her sight

00:06:38.639 --> 00:06:42.960
is restored she’s taken to the Hall of Faces,
which the Faceless Men use to assume false

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:48.740
identities. Arya becomes “The Ugly Little
Girl” and Mercy. Arya is ordered to kill

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:53.869
an insurance man, which she does, in the books,
but she also kills some targets of her own.

00:06:53.869 --> 00:06:59.099
She kills Dareon, a Night’s Watchman who’s
breaking his vows, and kills Raff the Sweetling,

00:06:59.099 --> 00:07:03.559
one of Gregor Clegane’s men, from her list.
In the show it’s Meryn Trant instead, but

00:07:03.559 --> 00:07:10.339
the kill is similar. So that’s Arya’s
story so far. In these first five books and

00:07:10.339 --> 00:07:15.319
seasons, she’s gone from a sweet kid to
a vicious assassin. She’s lost everything.

00:07:15.319 --> 00:07:22.119
Her family, her friends, and her sense of
self. What will happen next? Where can she go from here?

00:07:22.119 --> 00:07:28.330
She’ll obviously probably be doing some
killing, and the people on her list are the

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:33.990
obvious targets. But they’re all down south,
involved in other stuff. Where Arya really

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:40.460
wants to go is north, to the Wall, to Jon. Arya and Jon think of each other all the

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:44.659
time. Arya only goes to Braavos cause
the ship can’t take her to Jon, and much

00:07:44.659 --> 00:07:50.360
of Jon’s story in Dance is about Arya – the
plot with Mance, the decision to ride south.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.699
Of course, Jon is stabbed pretty bad, but
there’s strong evidence he’ll be resurrected

00:07:54.699 --> 00:08:00.129
by Melisandre – who in the show, meets Arya
and tells her they’ll meet again. Anyway

00:08:00.129 --> 00:08:04.909
maybe the Faceless Men, as worshippers of
death, disapprove of Jon’s resurrection,

00:08:04.909 --> 00:08:10.469
and send Arya to have him killed a second
time. Maybe Arya will wear the face of Jeyne

00:08:10.469 --> 00:08:15.619
Poole, who, in the books, is used by the Boltons
as a fake Arya to marry Ramsay, so Arya may

00:08:15.619 --> 00:08:20.939
impersonate the person who impersonated her.
It’s implied that Faceless Men aren’t

00:08:20.939 --> 00:08:25.270
allowed to kill people whose names they know, though, so Arya might only be sent to kill

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:30.969
Jon if Snow goes by Azor Ahai or King Jonathon
Starkgaryen the First or whatever. But the

00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:36.089
point – is – imagine the drama of Arya
being sent to kill Jon. It could be the big

00:08:36.089 --> 00:08:41.620
test of whether Arya truly is no one – could
she bring herself to kill her beloved brother,

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:46.399
the last of her family that she knows of?
Could she truly let go of her identity as

00:08:46.399 --> 00:08:52.029
Arya? The answer is probably no. The kindly
man says “[he doesn’t] think [Arya] can”

00:08:52.029 --> 00:08:56.040
become no one, that beneath all her names,
all her identities, there’s still some Arya

00:08:56.040 --> 00:09:00.870
there, and it looks like he’s right, Arya
says as much herself. She doesn’t kill

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:06.019
for the Many-Faced God, she kills to avenge
her friends and family. And she keeps Needle.

00:09:06.019 --> 00:09:13.350
“Try as she might … she [cannot] rid herself
of Arya”, can’t become no one.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:18.079
So will she go back to being Arya? What’s
left to go back to? Arya’s “home [is]

00:09:18.079 --> 00:09:22.870
gone, her parents dead, and all her brothers
slain but Jon”, plus tree-boy Bran and

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:27.750
unicorn-island Rickon. And what’s even left
of Arya? She’s been Horseface, Underfoot,

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:32.360
Arry, Lumpyhead, Lumpyface, Weasel, Nan,
Squab, Salty, Cat, Blind Beth, “The Ugly

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:38.259
Little Girl”, Mercy… and each one has
worn away at her identity. Like “the kindly

00:09:38.259 --> 00:09:43.779
man” says, there is an Arya beneath all
this, but this Arya is so… broken. She says

00:09:43.779 --> 00:09:48.339
she has a “hole inside her where her heart
had been”, that “The hole will never feel

00:09:48.339 --> 00:09:54.139
any better”. Arya is extremely tough and
adaptable, but she’s an eleven-year-old

00:09:54.139 --> 00:09:58.880
girl. Her family and friends have been butchered
before her, she’s seen murder and worse

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:03.490
at Harrenhal, her best friend is “the worst
shit in the Seven Kingdoms”, and she joins

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:09.230
a literal death cult. She’s deeply traumatised,
part of why she tries to forget her life as

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:13.860
Arya is to dissociate from her suffering. After
all she’s been through, Arya can hardly

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.690
function like a person, let alone become
the noble lady she never wanted to be in the

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:23.730
first place. She can’t trust, she can’t
relax, all she knows is killing and survival.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:29.389
She can’t return to a normal life as Arya
Stark. But she can’t truly be “no one”,

00:10:29.389 --> 00:10:36.940
either. Who or what can she be?
Arya is connected to the old gods, the “nameless,

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:41.279
faceless gods of the greenwood”. She feels
them guiding her steps, and when she prays

00:10:41.279 --> 00:10:45.860
to them in Clash, she hears a response. She
hears her father’s voice repeating

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:51.769
“When the snows fall and the white winds
blow, the lone wolf dies, but the pack survives”,

00:10:51.769 --> 00:10:56.490
she is reminded that she has “The wolf blood”,
and she hears a “great pack” of wolves,

00:10:56.490 --> 00:11:01.730
“calling to [her]”. Arya is closely associated
with wolves throughout the series. People

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:05.610
call her a “wolf girl” and a “wolf bitch”. She sees wolves, she hears wolves, she

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:11.110
howls to wolves and they howl back. She thinks
of herself as a wolf. In fact, Arya is a

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:16.199
warg, someone who enters the minds of animals, like Bran enters Summer. She wargs a couple

00:11:16.199 --> 00:11:22.160
of cats in Braavos, but mostly wargs her
direwolf, Nymeria. She has wolf dreams, meaning

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:27.379
while she sleeps, her mind becomes one with
Nymeria, who now leads a “great pack [of]

00:11:27.379 --> 00:11:32.350
hundreds of … mankill[ing wolves]” around
the riverlands. Arya wolf dreams all

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:37.610
the time, more and more as the series goes
on, and this forms a new identity, different

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:42.690
to Arya and different to “no one” – she
calls herself the “night wolf”. And this

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:48.410
is what she wants. Arya wishes and prays
to be made into a wolf. And there actually

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:54.470
is a way that could happen.
We know from the prologue of Dance that when

00:11:54.470 --> 00:12:00.660
a warg, like Arya, dies, they may live a second
life by having their spirit leave their body

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:07.230
and become one with their animal. If Arya
dies, her spirit could become one with Nymeria.

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:12.769
There’s plenty of foreshadowing that Arya
may die. Ned compares Arya to her aunt Lyanna,

00:12:12.769 --> 00:12:18.800
who had “The wolf blood”, was “willful,
and dead before her time”. Jon jokes that

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:23.350
after winter, “they will find [Arya’s]
body with a needle still locked tight between

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:28.500
[her] frozen fingers”. And we’ve heard
over and over from Arya and others that “valar

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:33.040
morghulis” – all men must die. George
R. R. Martin has said that the ending of his

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:38.079
series will be bittersweet. The death of
Arya would be tragic, but it’d be sweet

00:12:38.079 --> 00:12:43.389
in that Arya would finally have what she’s
wanted all this time. Cause in one sense, Arya’s

00:12:43.389 --> 00:12:47.889
story is about a killer’s quest to take
revenge on evil men, but it’s also the story

00:12:47.889 --> 00:12:53.439
of a kid trying to find a family, what Arya
calls a pack. This is what Arya’s been

00:12:53.439 --> 00:12:57.459
chasing all this time, it’s why she sticks
with Hot Pie and Gendy even when she’d be

00:12:57.459 --> 00:13:01.829
safer alone, why she stays with the Hound,
when he murdered her friend, maybe even

00:13:01.829 --> 00:13:06.189
why she joins the Faceless Men. There’s
no denying that Arya is a killer, but she

00:13:06.189 --> 00:13:11.649
also wants a pack, at least as much as she
wants blood, and becoming Nymeria could give

00:13:11.649 --> 00:13:18.180
her both. She’d be “swift and strong,
running down her prey with her pack at her

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:22.699
heels”. Arya dying and becoming Nymeria
would fulfil Ned’s words of “the lone

00:13:22.699 --> 00:13:27.470
wolf [dying], but the pack [surviving]”,
it would solve Arya’s identity crisis by

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:31.579
becoming the “night wolf” rather than
Arya or “no one”, and it would give a

00:13:31.579 --> 00:13:38.129
beautiful bittersweet ending to a story of
loss of identity and death. A working title

00:13:38.129 --> 00:13:43.249
for the final instalment of the series was
A Time for Wolves. You can almost see the

00:13:43.249 --> 00:13:49.339
epilogue, the closing moment of the series,
after all the misery maybe we’ll see Arya,

00:13:49.339 --> 00:13:54.949
as a direwolf, running with her pack across
the snow.

00:13:54.949 --> 00:13:59.089
So feel free to comment what you think will
happen to Arya, and subscribe to Alt Shift

00:13:59.089 --> 00:14:02.850
X for more videos on Game of Thrones and more.
Thanks.

